## 86. Comparison Chart

| Concept | Fast Rule | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| Opposite | Never shares an edge | Low |
| Adjacent | Shares an edge | Low |
| Corner | Exactly 3 faces | Low |
| Common edge | Compare third faces | Medium |
| Rotation | Preserve orientation | Medium |
| Reflection | Reverses orientation | High |
| Standard die | Opposite sum 7 | Low if truly standard |
| Net | Fold mentally | Medium |
| Roll | Track position cycle | Medium |

---

## 87. Mental Visualization Drill

Train yourself by imagining a labelled cube:

```text
        1
     4  2  3
        6
```

with `5` behind 2.

Now mentally ask:

```text
What is opposite 1? → 6
What is opposite 2? → 5
What is opposite 3? → 4
Which faces touch 2? → 1,3,4,6
```

Do this repeatedly until the cube becomes automatic in your mind.

---

## 88. Final Master Summary

The entire chapter can be compressed to:

```text
                 DICE REASONING
                       |
       ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐
       ↓               ↓                ↓
   OPPOSITE         ADJACENT         ROTATION
       |               |                |
   1 face          4 faces          positions move
       |               |                |
 never touches     shares edge       opposites stay
       |                                |
       └──────────────┬─────────────────┘
                      ↓
                  CORNERS
                      |
                3 faces meet
                      |
           no opposite pair allowed
                      |
                      ↓
                 ORIENTATION
                      |
             rotation ≠ reflection
```

